      "writtenOn": "2021-01-19T16:37:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of these try/catches and conversions to int, suggest:\n\n    private void synchronizeKernelRCU() throws ErrnoException {\n        // This is a temporary hack for network stats map swap on devices running\n        // 4.9 kernels. The kernel code of socket release on pf_key socket will\n        // explicitly call synchronize_rcu() which is exactly what we need.\n        // TODO: use something better on newer kernels, such as map-in-map swaps.\n        FileDescriptor pfSocket \u003d Os.socket(AF_KEY,\n                OsConstants.SOCK_RAW | OsConstants.SOCK_CLOEXEC, PF_KEY_V2);\n        // When closing socket, synchronize_rcu() gets called in sock_release().\n        Os.close(pfSocket);\n    }\n\nThen in the caller, you can do:\n\n    try {\n        synchronizeKernelRCU();\n    } catch (ErrnoException e) {\n        mLog.e(\"synchronizeKernelRCU: \" + e);\n    }\n\nIf you look at the string representation of ErrnoException, it does:\n\n        String description \u003d Libcore.os.strerror(errno);\n        if (errnoName \u003d\u003d null) {\n            errnoName \u003d \"errno \" + errno;\n        }\n        return functionName + \" failed: \" + errnoName + \" (\" + description + \")\";\n\nso you\u0027ll end up logging something like:\n\n    \"synchronizeKernelRCU: socket failed: EPERM (Permission denied)\"\n\nand is enough to debug the error.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 273,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "6971e91d6284fbe14682cf88cf296e140b6192a2",
